  "prefLabel": "Phy 404.07 Extension of Conditionally Reinstated License When Supervised Practice is Incomplete or Supervisory Approval Letter is Unavailable",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Phy 404.07 Extension of Conditionally Reinstated License When Supervised Practice is Incomplete or Supervisory Approval Letter is Unavailable. The OPLC shall extend a conditionally reinstated license for an additional period of no more than 26 weeks when:\n\n(a) The conditionally reinstated license is still valid;\n\n(b) The licensee holding the conditionally reinstated license:\n\n(1) Is unable to complete the required supervised practice because of loss of employment for any reason other than being terminated for cause or terminated during probationary employment because of incompetence; or\n\n(2) Is unable to submit the required supervisory approval letter for a reason unrelated to the supervisor’s belief that they are not ready to practice under full licensure; and\n\n(c) The holder of the conditionally reinstated license submits to the OPLC a written request for the extension explaining the details of one of the reasons in (b) above.\n\nSource. #9431, eff 3-19-09; ss by #10402, eff 8-23-13; ss by #13825, eff 2-17-24 (formerly Phy 404.08)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/phy400.html"
}
